1
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:10,390
Amara's fitness watch draws a graph of her bike ride.

2
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:15,940
A steep section, then a flat section, then a less steep section back home.

3
00:00:15,990 --> 00:00:20,380
What does the flat section mean: she stopped, or she was fastest?

4
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:23,620
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:23,670 --> 00:00:24,440
She stopped.

6
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:28,900
Time goes on, but her distance from home does not change.

7
00:00:28,950 --> 00:00:32,810
Remember: speed equals distance divided by time.

8
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:36,400
On a distance-time graph, the gradient is the speed.

9
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:37,850
Steeper means faster.

10
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:40,550
Sloping down means coming back.

11
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,410
Out: 10 kilometres in 20 minutes.

12
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:50,390
20 minutes is a third of an hour, so 10 times 3 is 30 kilometres per hour.

13
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:51,070
Your turn.

14
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:54,820
Find her speed on the way back, in kilometres per hour.

15
00:00:54,870 --> 00:00:58,070
Pause the video and try it.

16
00:00:58,120 --> 00:01:02,700
Back: 10 kilometres in 30 minutes, which is half an hour.

17
00:01:02,750 --> 00:01:07,070
10 divided by a half is 20 kilometres per hour.

18
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:11,370
A straight line through the origin gives an equation.

19
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:16,880
A runner covers 240 metres in 100 seconds, so D equals 2.4 T.

20
00:01:16,930 --> 00:01:20,670
On a cost graph, the gradient is the price for each item.

21
00:01:20,720 --> 00:01:23,940
On a tank graph, it is litres per minute.

22
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:25,300
Here is the method.

23
00:01:25,350 --> 00:01:28,420
Step 1: read the axes and the units.

24
00:01:28,470 --> 00:01:32,480
Step 2: describe each section: up, flat, or down.

25
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:36,320
Step 3: gradient equals change up over change across.

26
00:01:36,370 --> 00:01:38,100
That is the rate.

27
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:42,010
Step 4: check the units, like minutes or hours.

28
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:48,700
Three sections: 4 kilometres in 10 minutes, 6 in 20 minutes, 3 in 5 minutes.

29
00:01:48,750 --> 00:01:50,990
Per minute: 0.4, 0.3, 0.6.

30
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:53,390
The third is fastest.

31
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:57,100
A taxi graph goes through 0, 3 and 10, 23.

32
00:01:57,150 --> 00:02:00,550
The gradient is 20 over 10, which is 2.

33
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:03,140
So C equals 2 D plus 3.

34
00:02:03,190 --> 00:02:03,930
Your turn.

35
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:05,110
D equals 2.4 T.

36
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:07,410
Find D when T is 900 seconds.

37
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:10,550
Pause and work it out.

38
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:16,780
2.4 times 900 is 2,160 metres, if she keeps the same speed.

39
00:02:16,830 --> 00:02:20,570
At the flat section, Amara is 10 kilometres from home.

40
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:21,980
Leo reads the graph.

41
00:02:22,030 --> 00:02:23,930
Which line is wrong?

42
00:02:23,980 --> 00:02:25,080
Line 1 is wrong.

43
00:02:25,130 --> 00:02:27,030
The height is the distance.

44
00:02:27,080 --> 00:02:29,450
The speed is the gradient.

45
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:31,180
Flat means a speed of 0.

46
00:02:31,230 --> 00:02:32,880
She has stopped.

47
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:42,100
Delivery apps and smart energy meters show graphs where the gradient is a rate: kilometres per hour, or kilowatt hours per day.

48
00:02:42,150 --> 00:02:43,450
One last question.

49
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:47,490
A tank fills from 30 litres to 90 litres in 4 minutes.

50
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:50,410
What is the rate, in litres per minute?

51
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:53,840
Pause the video and answer.

52
00:02:53,890 --> 00:02:58,560
60 litres in 4 minutes is 15 litres per minute.

53
00:02:58,610 --> 00:03:01,120
To remember: the gradient is the rate.

54
00:03:01,170 --> 00:03:04,490
On a distance-time graph, it is the speed.

55
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,000
Flat means no change.

56
00:03:06,050 --> 00:03:08,060
Steeper means faster.

57
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:10,290
Check the units.

58
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:14,140
Straight lines give equations for predictions.

59
00:03:14,190 --> 00:03:19,550
Great work! Now practise lesson 10.4 on Camday.
